'@ | Set-Content .env.example

@'
# Research Library

Flask + SQLAlchemy backend (uv) and Vite React/TypeScript frontend.

## Windows setup

Install with winget (PowerShell):

    winget install Python.Python.3.12
    winget install OpenJS.NodeJS.LTS
    winget install Git.Git
    winget install astral-sh.uv
    winget install UB-Mannheim.TesseractOCR

Add `C:\Program Files\Tesseract-OCR` to your user PATH, then check:

    tesseract --version
    tesseract --list-langs    # must include "eng"

If PowerShell blocks npm:

    Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope CurrentUser -ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned

Optional: keep uv and model caches on the same drive as the repo (set `UV_CACHE_DIR` and `HF_HOME`).

## Install from lockfiles

    cd backend;  uv sync --locked
    cd frontend; npm ci

## Run tests

    cd backend;  uv run pytest
    cd frontend; npm test

## Start

    cd backend;  uv run flask --app app run --debug
    cd frontend; npm run dev

Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and adjust. Put private PDFs in `papers/` (git-ignored).
'@ | Set-Content README.md